IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc-definitions`
IMPORT `ccc14-part122-disclosure`

-- ccc14-tests-part122-disclosure.l4 -- tests for ccc14-part122-disclosure.l4 (Criminal Code, ss 462.47 to 462.5).
-- Every expected value is written from the text of the section named beside it, before the run; none is copied from the module's output.
-- The conjunction cases (every condition TRUE gives the answer; each condition FALSE in turn gives the other answer) are typed by work/gen_tests_disclosure.py from a table of expectations.
-- Y = JUST TRUE; N = JUST FALSE; NA = NOTHING (not covered).

`ccc14 Y` MEANS JUST TRUE
`ccc14 N` MEANS JUST FALSE

GIVEN s IS A NUMBER, sub IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Provision of the Code`
`ccc14 test at` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF s, sub

§ `s 462.47 -- No civil or criminal liability incurred by informants`
-- args: discloses to a peace officer or the Attorney General; the facts are the basis of a reasonable suspicion; section 241 of the Income Tax Act prevents the disclosure
#ASSERT `s 462.47 the person is justified in disclosing the facts to a peace officer or the Attorney General` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ccc14 Y`
#ASSERT `s 462.47 the person is justified in disclosing the facts to a peace officer or the Attorney General` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 462.47 the person is justified in disclosing the facts to a peace officer or the Attorney General` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 462.47 the person is justified in disclosing the facts to a peace officer or the Attorney General` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

